# UF Scheduling Assistant — Project Context

## Purpose
LLM-powered FastAPI microservice that helps UF students research courses. Aggregates data from four sources: UF One.UF Schedule of Courses API (live), RateMyProfessors (GraphQL), r/UFL Reddit posts (SQLite FTS5 index), and GatorEvals (offline CSVs). Exposes SSE-based AI chat, a public chat room, user profiles, and usage metrics — all persisted to **Amazon DynamoDB**.

## Architecture

```
main.py                         (FastAPI app + lifespan — uvicorn main:app)
chat.py                         (build_agent() — LangGraph ReAct agent + tools + CLI loop)
tui.py                          (Textual-based TUI demo)
api/                            (API package)
  __init__.py
  routers/
    __init__.py                 (aggregates all sub-routers)
    health.py                   (GET /health)
    ai_chat.py                  (POST /ai-chat, GET history & detail, DELETE session)
    chat_room.py                (SSE stream, send/load messages)
    active_users.py             (GET /active-users/stream — unauthenticated SSE)
    metrics.py                  (POST major/course/search tracking)
    user.py                     (POST /users/username, GET /users/me)
  controllers/
    ai_chat.py                  (AI chat business logic, SSE streaming, tool_call events)
    chat_room.py                (pub/sub chat room, DynamoDB persistence)
    active_users.py             (in-memory active-user presence tracking)
    metrics.py                  (daily analytics counters)
    user.py                     (user management — DynamoDB ufscheduler-users)
  models/
    __init__.py                 (re-exports all Pydantic models)
    ai_chat.py                  (ChatRequest, ChatDeleteResponse, ChatSummary,
                                 ChatHistoryResponse, ChatDetailMessage, ChatDetailResponse)
    health.py                   (HealthResponse)
    chat_room.py                (SendMessageRequest, ChatMessage, LoadMessagesResponse)
    metrics.py                  (TrackMajorRequest, TrackCourseRequest, TrackSearchRequest,
                                 MetricsResponse)
    user.py                     (SetUsernameRequest, SetUsernameResponse, UserProfile)
tools/                          (@tool-decorated LangChain tool functions)
  course_search.py              (UF SOC live API — calls course_data.py)
  course_data.py                (term auto-detection, One.UF API requests)
  rmp_search.py                 (RateMyProfessors GraphQL)
  reddit_search.py              (SQLite FTS5 + vulgarity filter)
  gatorevals_search.py          (offline CSV lookups from scrapers/gatorevals/)
  scheduler_actions.py          (CLIENT_ACTION_TOOLS — propose UI actions via tool_call SSE)
utils/
  auth.py                       (Cognito JWT validation via PyJWT + PyJWKClient)
  constants.py                  (env-driven config, table names, hardcoded limits)
  dynamo.py                     (DynamoDB resource + table handles)
  sessions.py                   (DynamoDB-backed AI chat session store — ufscheduler-ai-chats)
scrapers/                       (offline ETL — NOT part of the live request path)
  ufcoursecatalog.py            (bulk download UF SOC API → _clean.json)
  reddit_flair_scraper.py       (scrapes r/UFL by flair → UFL_master.json)
  run_reddit_scrapes.py         (orchestrator: initial / daily modes; state in reddit_scrapes/state/)
  reddit_db.py                  (SQLite DB helpers for FTS5 Reddit index)
  gatorevals/                   (GatorEvals scrapers + CSV outputs consumed by gatorevals_search.py)
  reddit_scrapes/
    master/UFL_reddit.db        (SQLite FTS5 database — updated nightly by GitHub Action)
    state/daily_progress.json
old-server/                     (Legacy Node/Express + Socket.io server — reference only)
```

## API Endpoints

| Method | Path | Auth | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/health` | None | `{"status": "ok"}` |
| `GET` | `/active-users/stream` | None | SSE: `active_users` events (in-memory presence) |
| `POST` | `/ai-chat` | Bearer JWT | Accepts `ChatRequest`; returns SSE stream |
| `GET` | `/ai-chat/history` | Bearer JWT | List `ChatSummary` objects for the authenticated user |
| `GET` | `/ai-chat/{session_id}` | Bearer JWT | Full session messages (`ChatDetailResponse`) |
| `DELETE` | `/ai-chat/{session_id}` | Bearer JWT | Deletes a session from DynamoDB |
| `GET` | `/chat-room/messages/stream` | Bearer JWT | SSE stream of new chat-room messages |
| `POST` | `/chat-room/messages` | Bearer JWT | Send a chat-room message (requires username) |
| `GET` | `/chat-room/messages` | None | Paginated message history (`last_evaluated_key` query param) |
| `POST` | `/metrics/major` | None | Track major selection |
| `POST` | `/metrics/course` | None | Track course view |
| `POST` | `/metrics/search` | None | Track search term |
| `POST` | `/users/username` | Bearer JWT | Set/update username (unique via GSI) |
| `GET` | `/users/me` | Bearer JWT | Return user profile from DynamoDB |

SSE event format (AI chat on `/ai-chat`):
```
event: token      data: {"token": "...", "session_id": "abc"}
event: tool_call  data: {"tool": "...", "args": {...}, "session_id": "abc"}   ← client-action tools only
event: done       data: {"session_id": "abc"}
event: error      data: {"detail": "..."}
```

## Key Conventions

- **Thin routes, fat controller:** routers in `api/routers/` are one-liners; all logic lives in `api/controllers/`
- **`from __future__ import annotations`** in every module
- **Tool outputs are plain text strings** — not JSON — so the LLM can interpret them directly
- **Global agent singleton:** `api.controllers.ai_chat.agent` is `None` at import time, set during FastAPI `lifespan`; never re-initialized per request
- **DynamoDB-backed sessions:** `utils/sessions.py` persists AI chat sessions to the `ufscheduler-ai-chats` table; in-memory sessions are gone
- **ContextVar for term isolation:** `course_data.set_request_term()` / `course_data.get_term()` use a `contextvars.ContextVar` so concurrent requests see their own semester code
- **Client-action tools never mutate server state** — `scheduler_actions.py` tools emit `tool_call` SSE events; the frontend confirms the action

## Environment Variables (from `.env` via `utils/constants.py`)

| Variable | Required | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | Yes | OpenAI key (`gpt-4o-mini`) |
| `COGNITO_REGION` | Yes | AWS region of Cognito user pool (also used for boto3) |
| `COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID` | Yes | Cognito User Pool ID (JWT issuer / JWKS URL) |
| `COGNITO_APP_CLIENT_ID` | Yes | JWT audience |
| `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | **Yes** | Comma-separated CORS origins — **app raises on startup if missing** |
| `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | No | Falls back to `~/.aws/credentials` for local dev |

Hardcoded in `utils/constants.py`: DynamoDB table names (`ufscheduler-chat`, `ufscheduler-users`, `ufscheduler-stats`, `ufscheduler-ai-chats`), `JWKS_TTL_SECONDS = 3600`, `MESSAGES_BATCH_SIZE`, `MESSAGE_MAX_LENGTH`, UF SOC base URL `https://one.uf.edu/apix/soc/schedule/`.

## Data Models

**`ChatRequest`** (`api/models/ai_chat.py`):
```python
prompt: str
session_id: str | None = None
```

**`ChatSummary`** / **`ChatHistoryResponse`** / **`ChatDetailResponse`** — returned by `/ai-chat/history` and `/ai-chat/{session_id}`.

**`SetUsernameRequest`** / **`UserProfile`** (`api/models/user.py`) — username uniqueness enforced via DynamoDB GSI `username-index`.

**DynamoDB document schemas:**

| Table | Key(s) | Key attributes |
|---|---|---|
| `ufscheduler-ai-chats` | `user_sub` (PK), `session_id` (SK) | `title`, `messages` (list of `{role, content}`), `created_at`, `updated_at` |
| `ufscheduler-users` | `sub` (PK) | `username`, `email`, `name`, `profilePic`, `createdAt`; GSI `username-index` |
| `ufscheduler-chat` | `id` (PK, value `"General"`), timestamp (SK) | `message`, `user`, `timestamp` |
| `ufscheduler-stats` | `type` (PK), `name` (SK) | `count`, `lastUpdated` |

**UF course dict** keys: `code`, `codeWithSpace`, `name`, `description`, `prerequisites`, `sections[]`  
Each section: `number`, `classNumber`, `sectWeb` (delivery mode), `instructors[]`, `meetTimes[]`, `credits_min`, `credits_max`, `genEd[]`, `quest[]`, `openSeats`, `waitList`, `courseFee`, `finalExam`, `note`, `deptName`

**Reddit post dict** keys: `id`, `title`, `selftext`, `author`, `created_utc`, `score`, `num_comments`, `flair`, `permalink`, `url`, `comments[]`

## Important Design Decisions

- **Live UF API:** `course_data.py` always queries `one.uf.edu` in real time — no local course cache.
- **Reddit:** Posts are stored in a SQLite database (`scrapers/reddit_scrapes/master/UFL_reddit.db`) and searched via FTS5 by `tools/reddit_search.py`. The DB is updated nightly by a GitHub Action (`.github/workflows/daily-reddit-scrape.yml`).
- **GatorEvals:** Implemented — `tools/gatorevals_search.py` reads offline CSVs produced by `scrapers/gatorevals/`. Not live-scraped per request.
- **DynamoDB sessions:** `utils/sessions.py` uses the `ufscheduler-ai-chats` table. Not suitable for multi-container deployments without sharing AWS credentials/region.
- **In-memory pub/sub:** `chat_room` and `active_users` controllers use in-memory subscriber sets — must be replaced with **Redis** (or similar) before running multiple ECS tasks.
- **JWKS rotation recovery:** If a `kid` is missing from the cache, `utils/auth.py` force-refreshes once before failing.
- **Vulgarity filtering:** `reddit_search.py` applies a compiled regex word-boundary filter before returning Reddit content to the LLM.
- **Term auto-detection:** `course_data.py` maps current month → UF term code (`Spring=1-4`, `Summer=5-7`, `Fall=8-12`) encoded as `2{YY}{sem}` (e.g. Spring 2026 = `"2261"`). Per-request isolation via `ContextVar`.
- **`chat.py` doubles as a CLI:** `main()` provides a terminal loop for quick local testing without running the full API. `tui.py` provides a richer Textual TUI.
- **Auth library:** `PyJWT` + `PyJWKClient` (not `python-jose`).
- **Migration from Node:** `old-server/server.js` (Express + Socket.io) is retained as reference; DynamoDB table structure and metrics patterns were ported to the Python controllers.

## Scrapers (offline ETL — do not modify unless working on data pipeline)

- `scrapers/ufcoursecatalog.py` — bulk download UF SOC API → `_clean.json`
- `scrapers/reddit_flair_scraper.py` — scrapes r/UFL by flair (Classes, Schedule, Graduation) → `UFL_master.json`
- `scrapers/run_reddit_scrapes.py` — orchestrator for `initial` (50-day backfill) / `daily` (3-day) modes; tracks state in `reddit_scrapes/state/daily_progress.json`
- `scrapers/reddit_db.py` — SQLite + FTS5 helpers
- `scrapers/gatorevals/` — GatorEvals scraper scripts + CSV outputs consumed by `tools/gatorevals_search.py`

## CI / Deployment

**GitHub Actions:** `.github/workflows/daily-reddit-scrape.yml` runs `python run_reddit_scrapes.py daily` on a cron and commits the updated `UFL_reddit.db` back to the repo.

**Docker:** Python 3.12-slim, port 8000, health check on `/health`, non-root user, `uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000`  
**Makefile targets:** `make build`, `make run` (docker + `--env-file .env`), `make run-mount` (dev with volume), `make stop`, `make dev` (local uvicorn with `--reload`)
